{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LIVE EXECUTION EVIDENCE — the job result I promised to record before closing.\n\nGitHub Actions run **30660546548**, job **\"jira DC harness smoke (real Jira Data Center, ephemeral)\"**,\nagainst main @ fde6baae7 (which contains this story's merged change, f1a14e0c5).\n\n    [jira-live-canary] collected=17 executed=17 skipped=0\n    1 failed, 16 passed in 13.55s\n\n`executed=17 skipped=0` is the load-bearing line, not the pass count: it proves nothing silently\nskipped, so the all-skip canary this tier exists to satisfy has nothing to hide. The documented\ncommands were genuinely RUN against a real Jira Data Center instance.\n\nTHE CRITERION'S EXECUTION HALF — MET.\n`test_the_documented_config_and_dry_run_work_against_a_real_dc_instance` **PASSED**. It lifts the\n`[tool.rebar.reconciler]` TOML block OUT of `docs/user-guide.md` at runtime (rather than restating it,\nso the guide and the test cannot drift), writes it as a `pyproject.toml` — the surface on which the\ndocumented `[tool.rebar.…]` spelling actually applies (`_config_sources.py:111-115`) — exports\n`JIRA_PAT`, and runs the documented `rebar reconcile --dry-run`. It asserts a `no_write` envelope and\n`mutation_failures == 0`, not merely exit 0, because a guide that says \"inspect before enabling live\nsync\" and then WRITES would be actively dangerous.\n\nThe harness-free half of the criterion (`pip install 'nava-rebar[jira-datacenter]'` names a real\ndistribution and a really-declared extra) is checked by `tests/unit/test_user_guide_dc_docs.py`, which\nruns on every change rather than only when a Dockerized Jira is available.\n\nTHE ONE FAILURE IN THAT RUN, AND WHY IT IS NOT AN OBJECTION TO CLOSING.\n`test_the_documented_setup_refuses_to_read_the_pat_from_config` — also one of this story's tests —\nfailed. It did not fail because the documentation is wrong; it failed because it CAUGHT A REAL PRODUCT\nDEFECT: with `JIRA_PAT` absent from the environment and present only in config, the reconciler fell\nback to ANONYMOUS access instead of failing with an error naming the variable, contradicting a\nsecurity property the guide states. That is filed and FIXED as [rebar:cd78-d877-3d25-4ec3], merged as\nchange 1127 (`ed9d5e28d`). The test doing its job is evidence the documentation is being enforced, not\nevidence that this story is incomplete.\n\nA confirming run against the first main containing that fix (run 30662366152, main @ ed9d5e28d) is in\nflight; its result will be appended here. Reading the JOB rather than the overall run status\nthroughout, as this ticket's earlier comment committed to — the overall run is red for the unrelated\nlive-LLM tier."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785529375247853001,"uuid":"41ac3d9e-e43b-41f1-be90-299960274f5f"}